The mass general strike has crippled the Commonwealth economy, bringing the country to a complete standstill. With the the Banners strong and organized, the government cannot simply crush the hundreds of thousands of <span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span> protesters flooding the streets.

Meanwhile, in defiance of the indefinite adjournment of the Assembly, the <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> parties have banded together to unofficially reconvene the chamber at a separate location, openly challenging federal authority.

The next few days will be chaotic—and decisive for the Commonwealth as a whole.

- @z_break
- @schleicher_cabinet_13_pre_pre

